{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that explores the fascinating story of facebook's creation and the tumultuous journey of its founder, mark zuckerberg. directed by david fincher, the film is a riveting and thought-provoking drama that delves into the complexities of ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard, creating a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. this initial spark of creativity sets off a chain reaction that eventually leads to the creation of facebook. as the site gains popularity, zuckerberg is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who claim that he stole their idea for a social networking site.\n\nthe film's narrative is presented in a non-linear fashion, jumping back and forth between zuckerberg's time at harvard and the subsequent lawsuits and controversies that surround him. this non-linear structure adds to the movie's complexity and keeps the viewer engaged.\n\nthe cast of the movie delivers outstanding performances, with jesse eisenberg shining as the complex and often unlikeable mark zuckerberg. eisenberg brings a depth and nuance to the character, capturing both his intelligence and his awkwardness. andrew garfield and justin timberlake also deliver strong performances as eduardo saverin and sean parker, respectively.\n\none of the most striking aspects of the movie is its exploration of the themes of friendship and betrayal. the relationship between zuckerberg and saverin is particularly well-portrayed, with the two characters navigating the challenges of their partnership and ultimately succumbing to the pressures of success.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. the soundtrack is a haunting and atmospheric blend of electronic and ambient music that perfectly captures the mood and tone of the movie.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that offers a fascinating glimpse into the world of tech entrepreneurship and the complexities of success. while some viewers may take issue with the movie's portrayal of mark zuckerberg and the events surrounding facebook's creation, the film is undeniably a compelling and well-crafted drama that is sure to leave a lasting impression.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.9773347973823547}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0004104725376237184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.01104797888547182}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -2.65096378326416}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0052891322411596775}, {"token": " explores", "logprob": -1.0755043029785156}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fascinating", "logprob": -1.5779002904891968}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -0.011076745577156544}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.018149960786104202}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.21022439002990723}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.0016255272785201669}, {"token": " creation", "logprob": -0.09571044892072678}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.08118155598640442}, {"token": " tumult", "logprob": -0.47770506143569946}, {"token": "uous", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " journey", "logprob": -0.3631976842880249}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " its", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " founder", "logprob": -0.004181927070021629}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00033539868309162557}, {"token": " mark", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " zu", "logprob": -4.410734163684538e-06}, {"token": "cker", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "berg", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.0005184260080568492}, {"toke